  "summary": "Traditional Slovak embroidery featuring geometric patterns and floral motifs in vibrant colors.",
  "description": "Detva and Slovacko embroidery consists of intricate geometric and floral designs executed in bright red, blue, green, and yellow threads on white or colored fabric, often covering entire garments. This embroidery style developed in central Slovakia as part of traditional folk costumes, with each region developing distinctive patterns that reflected local identity, while the geometric precision demonstrated the artisan's skill and adherence to traditional techniques passed down through generations.",
